WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.820
Will Black Adam and Shazam ever clash on screen?&nbsp;
It has almost happened a couple times, but one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.440
person stood in the way: Dwayne Johnson. Here's&nbsp;
why he put the kibosh on this clash of the titans.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.460
The 2022 release of "Black Adam" was&nbsp;
the culmination of years of production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.180
beginning with Dwayne Johnson being cast&nbsp;
in the titular role all the way back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.640
2007. Black Adam's arrival on the big screen&nbsp;
was preceded by the 2019 film "Shazam!" That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.900
film followed the story of a foster child named&nbsp;
Billy Batson who gets infused with superpowers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.940
including flight and invulnerability, by a&nbsp;
wizard. In the comics, Shazam and Black Adam are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.260
arch-enemies who got their powers from the same&nbsp;
source, but opted for different paths afterward.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.739
"I kneel before no one."

00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:40.058
"Get me out of here!"

00:00:40.111 --> 00:00:44.280
With both characters now officially in the&nbsp;
DC Extended Universe, many comic book fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.700
have been eager to see the two square off&nbsp;
against one another. But it appears that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.020
confrontation isn't happening any time soon.&nbsp;
Johnson has reportedly nixed a planned Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.160
Adam appearance in the "Shazam!" sequel,&nbsp;
"Shazam! Fury of the Gods." Film reporter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.860
Umberto Gonzalez tweeted,&nbsp;
using Johnson's nickname,

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.960
Johnson's decision isn't necessarily a surprise.&nbsp;
He doesn't seem to be big on the character of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.120
Shazam, despite his historical connection to&nbsp;
Black Adam. The 2019 film "Shazam!" was poised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.720
to introduce Black Adam in a scene where the&nbsp;
newly superpowered members of the Shazam family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.160
sat on their thrones before realizing there&nbsp;
was a seventh seat that sat empty. The Wrap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.420
reported that Johnson quashed the scene, as well&nbsp;
as any other reference to Black Adam in the film.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:29.400
In an August 2022 Vanity Fair interview, Johnson&nbsp;
confirmed that Black Adam originally had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.180
prominent part in "Shazam!" He noted that&nbsp;
the script originally served as an origin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.200
story for both characters, but he wasn't&nbsp;
open to such an arrangement. He explained,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.380
Johnson said that he made a call to Warner&nbsp;
Bros. executives and insisted they separate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.400
the characters, allowing "Shazam!" to develop&nbsp;
its own tone independent of Black Adam.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.471
"The hierarchy of power in the&nbsp;
DC universe is about to change."

00:02:01.471 --> 00:02:06.960
Fandom Wire caught up with Zachary Levi, who plays&nbsp;
Shazam, at Comic Con Portugal in December 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.800
and asked him about whether Black Adam&nbsp;
and Shazam would meet on screen. Levi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.520
responded that he has no idea whether the two&nbsp;
characters would get a chance to interact and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.300
has no influence over how the story would&nbsp;
play out. He did playfully point out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.260
though, that if he had the opportunity to punch&nbsp;
Dwayne Johnson in the face, he would take it.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.380
The Hollywood Reporter called a&nbsp;
sequel to "Black Adam" "unlikely"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.740
now that James Gunn and Peter Safran&nbsp;
have taken over as the new heads of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:32.940
DC studios. It's one of a slate of planned&nbsp;
projects the two have reportedly scrapped.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:37.200
While on stage at Comic Con Portugal, Levi&nbsp;
was asked about his own character's cinematic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.160
future. Levi responded that Gunn and Safran&nbsp;
are friends of his and joked that friendship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.180
would be in jeopardy if they didn't have Shazam&nbsp;
as a part of their plans for DC going forward.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.740
In an interview with Collider, "Shazam!" and&nbsp;
"Shazam! Fury Of The Gods" director David F.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:54.420
Sandberg was also asked about plans for Black&nbsp;
Adam and Shazam to interact in future films. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.900
responded that he has not been involved in&nbsp;
any conversations about the two characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.220
coming face to face, adding that both characters&nbsp;
were on their own trajectories at the moment.

